## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design an end-to-end Snowflake ELT for semi-structured logs, including external stages, staging vs. target tables, and simple QC/alerting.

## Key Concepts

- External stages and JSON formats
- Staging vs. target tables
- COPY INTO and data transformation
- TASK scheduling and QC views
- Simple alerting pattern

## Code Example

```sql
CREATE FILE FORMAT jsonfmt TYPE=JSON;
CREATE STAGE s3_logs URL='s3://logs-bucket/app-logs/';
CREATE TABLE LOGS_STG(timestamp_str STRING, user_id STRING, event_type STRING, payload VARIANT);
CREATE TABLE LOGS(timestamp_ntz TIMESTAMP_NTZ, user_id STRING, event_type STRING, payload VARIANT);
COPY INTO LOGS_STG FROM @s3_logs PATTERN='.*app_log.json' FILE_FORMAT=(FORMAT_NAME='jsonfmt');
INSERT INTO LOGS SELECT to_timestamp_ntz(timestamp_str), user_id, event_type, payload FROM LOGS_STG;
CREATE VIEW LOGS_QC AS SELECT date_trunc('DAY', timestamp_ntz) day, COUNT(DISTINCT user_id) users, COUNT(*) events FROM LOGS GROUP BY 1;
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema drift in JSON payloads?
- How would you adjust the pipeline for new fields or partitions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of data protection basics in Snowflake using masking policies and role-based access. It also covers applying policies, privilege grants, and simple auditing.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic data masking with MASKING POLICY
- CURRENT_ROLE() for access decisions
- GRANT/REVOKE science for roles
- Auditing access via QA tables

## Code Example
```javascript
CREATE MASKING POLICY budget_masking AS (val NUMBER) RETURNS NUMBER ->
CASE WHEN (CURRENT_ROLE() IN ('FINANCE_ROLE')) THEN val ELSE 0 END;

ALTER TABLE PUBLIC.PROJECT_BUDGET MODIFY COLUMN budget SET MASKING POLICY budget_masking;

CREATE ROLE FINANCE_ROLE;
CREATE ROLE ANALYST_ROLE;
GRANT USAGE ON DATABASE <DB> TO ROLE ANALYST_ROLE;
GRANT SELECT ON PUBLIC.PROJECT_BUDGET TO ROLE ANALYST_ROLE;
GRANT USAGE ON DATABASE <DB> TO ROLE FINANCE_ROLE;
GRANT SELECT ON PUBLIC.PROJECT_BUDGET TO ROLE FINANCE_ROLE;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What are potential pitfalls with masking policies in shared datasets?
- How would you test masking policy behavior across multiple roles?
